   "partialWhy": "Both of its books, and neither of them from the Ge'ez in full. The second, the discourse of the risen Lord, is James's English of the Ethiopic Guerrier published. The first, the church order, is here as the Syriac Testamentum Domini in Cooper and Maclean's English: the same work in another version, because the Ethiopic of it was unpublished when they wrote and has no public-domain English now.",
   "partialSource": "M. R. James, The Apocryphal New Testament, Oxford, 1924, pp. 485-503; J. Cooper and A. J. Maclean, The Testament of Our Lord, Edinburgh, 1902, pp. 47-138"
