   "present": false,
   "foldedInto": null,
   "absentWhy": "No public-domain English of the Ge'ez. The Ethiopic Zena Ayhud is a recension of the Hebrew Josippon, which reached English in 1558 in Peter Morwyng's translation and was reprinted into the eighteenth century — but that is the Hebrew, and the Ethiopic is an abridgement made through Arabic and differs from it substantially. Printing one as the other would be a bigger claim than this volume makes anywhere else.",
